OL,3,AHow the oil capital of the US welcomed
OL,4,Aa solar power boom
OL,5,
OL,6,FSteve Cargil's family has farmed the
OL,7,Fflat, dry land around Uvalde, a small
OL,8,Fcity in southwest Texas, since 1953.
OL,10,FCargil, 67, had always assumed that one
OL,11,Fof his three children would eventually
OL,12,Ftake it over, the way he had from his
OL,13,Ffather.
OL,15,FBut that assumption took a hit one
OL,16,Fnight in 2018 after a violent
OL,17,Fhailstorm.
OL,19,FCargil and his son, Ryan, had spent
OL,20,Fmonths nursing crops of cabbage and
OL,21,Fonions to harvest. Then a storm rolled
OL,22,Fthrough and destroyed them overnight.
